  "final_text": "**None of the eleven files works as evidence for R7.** The folder has no record of a restore test from the last 12 months. In fact, it has a record saying there wasn't one.\n\n| File | Why it doesn't work for R7 |\n|---|---|\n| `backup-report_2026-10.txt` | The closest match. It's current, has an owner (Goran Petrovski) and shows 31 of 31 backup jobs completed in October. But it says outright: *\"Restore test: not done in 2026. Planned for Q4 2026.\"* Successful backup jobs don't show that a restore works. |\n| `it-notes_2026-10-06.md` | Says \"Backups are tested\", but these are personal notes that nobody reviewed or approved. Tannwald says a description isn't enough. The note also conflicts with the backup report, which says no test was done. Don't send it as evidence. |\n| `infosec-policy_v3_FINAL.md` | Requires restore tests twice a year. That's a rule, not a record that a test happened. The policy is also out of date (approved 2024-03-12, review was due March 2025). It actually shows the gap: no test in 2026 breaches your own policy. |\n\nThe last 12 months go back to November 2025. The report only covers 2026, so a test in November or December 2025 is the one thing it doesn't rule out. Nothing in the folder suggests one happened, but it's worth asking Goran.\n\n**What I'd do:** The report already plans a restore test for Q4 2026, so run it before 25 November.\n- Restore a real backup: the Servicepult export, plus a sample from the file share.\n- Write it up with the date, what was restored, whether it worked, how long it took and any problems.\n- Have Goran (as owner) and Dragan Ilievski sign it.\n\nThat record is your R7 evidence. If the test can't happen by 25 November, tell Tannwald plainly: send the October backup report, say no restore test was done in 2026 and give the date it's scheduled. Don't use the IT notes to cover the gap. Tannwald will see the backup report at the audit, and claiming tests happened when the report says they didn't would do more damage than the gap itself.\n\nSome of the other R items have similar problems. I can go through R1–R8 if you want.",
